{% doc %}
  Puts a message on the next page.

  Why not modules/user/helpers/flash: that one runs t on what it is given,
  so it takes a translation key. Half the messages here are counted or
  interpolated, which means they have to be translated at the call site
  with arguments, and handing the result to a helper that translates again
  turns it into a blank string under safe_translate. This one takes the
  finished sentence.

  Writes the same {message, severity} shape the user module writes, so the
  host's own layout shows these too if an agent interface is ever embedded
  in one.

  @param {string} message - Already translated
  @param {string} [severity] - success, error or info. Defaults to info
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  if message == blank
    return null
  endif

  assign severity = severity | default: 'info'
  assign flash = { "message": message, "severity": severity, "from": context.location.pathname, "force_clear": false }

  function _ = 'modules/core/commands/session/set', key: 'sflash', value: flash
  return true
%}
